<figure class="wp-block-table alignwide is-style-discrepancy"><table><thead><tr><th>Detail</th><th>Mark</th><th>Matthew</th><th>Luke</th><th>John</th><th>Thomas</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Where it appears</td><td><code>15:1-47</code></td><td><code>27:1-66</code></td><td><code>23:1-56</code></td><td><code>18:28-19:42</code></td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>Day</td><td>The day after the Passover meal <code>14:12</code>; <code>15:42</code></td><td>The day after the Passover meal <code>26:17</code>; <code>27:62</code></td><td>The day after the Passover meal <code>22:7</code>; <code>23:54</code></td><td>The day of Preparation for the Passover <code>19:14,31</code></td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>The hour</td><td>The third hour <code>15:25</code></td><td>Not stated at the crucifixion; darkness from the sixth hour <code>27:45</code></td><td>Darkness from the sixth hour <code>23:44</code></td><td>About the sixth hour, Pilate gives judgment <code>19:14</code></td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>Who carries the cross</td><td>Simon of Cyrene <code>15:21</code></td><td>Simon of Cyrene <code>27:32</code></td><td>Simon of Cyrene <code>23:26</code></td><td>Jesus carries it himself <code>19:17</code></td><td>Saying 55 speaks of carrying the cross “as I do”, but tells no crucifixion</td></tr><tr><td>The notice</td><td>“The King of the Jews” <code>15:26</code></td><td>“This is Jesus the King of the Jews” <code>27:37</code></td><td>“This is the King of the Jews” <code>23:38</code></td><td>“Jesus of Nazareth, the King of the Jews”, in three languages <code>19:19-20</code></td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>The two others</td><td>Both revile him <code>15:32</code></td><td>Both revile him <code>27:44</code></td><td>One reviles; the other asks to be remembered <code>23:39-43</code></td><td>Present, and silent <code>19:18</code></td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>Words from the cross</td><td>“My God, my God, why have you forsaken me?” <code>15:34</code></td><td>“My God, my God, why have you forsaken me?” <code>27:46</code></td><td>“Father, into your hands I commit my spirit” <code>23:46</code></td><td>“It is finished” <code>19:30</code></td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>Women</td><td>Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James and Joses, and Salome, watching from a distance <code>15:40</code></td><td>Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James and Joseph, and the mother of Zebedee’s sons, from a distance <code>27:55-56</code></td><td>Those who had followed from Galilee, from a distance <code>23:49</code></td><td>Jesus’ mother, her sister, Mary of Clopas and Mary Magdalene, standing by the cross <code>19:25</code></td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>Temple curtain</td><td>Torn from top to bottom at his death <code>15:38</code></td><td>Torn at his death, with an earthquake and opened tombs <code>27:51-53</code></td><td>Torn before his death <code>23:45</code></td><td>Not mentioned</td><td>No account</td></tr><tr><td>Burial</td><td>Joseph of Arimathea <code>15:43-46</code></td><td>Joseph of Arimathea <code>27:57-60</code></td><td>Joseph of Arimathea <code>23:50-53</code></td><td>Joseph of Arimathea and Nicodemus <code>19:38-42</code></td><td>No account</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>
<!-- /wp:table -->
<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The gospels agree that Jesus was crucified under Pilate and buried by Joseph of Arimathea, and differ on the day, the hour, the cross, the last words and the women. Thomas has no passion narrative.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->
